WEBVTT

00:06.470 --> 00:07.480
Enemies?

00:07.480 --> 00:09.190
What nation's battleship is that?

00:09.660 --> 00:12.770
It probably belongs to 
the Bloodchain Brigade.

00:12.770 --> 00:15.320
What? The Bloodchain Brigade?

00:18.250 --> 00:21.510
So the rats scurried right into the trap?

00:21.510 --> 00:22.370
Rats?

00:22.820 --> 00:26.000
The Bloodchain Brigade are the most 
extreme of the anti-Highlander factions.

00:26.000 --> 00:30.890
They've been getting out of hand, 
and it's become a problem.

00:31.420 --> 00:33.580
So I set a trap.

00:33.950 --> 00:36.940
You knew about the Bloodchain Brigade?

00:36.940 --> 00:38.420
Obviously.

00:38.420 --> 00:40.040
A trap, you say?

00:40.040 --> 00:41.800
Nothing complicated.

00:41.800 --> 00:44.410
We just set up a fake ceremony.

00:44.410 --> 00:49.530
Then I, an Arch Lord, attended.

00:49.530 --> 00:51.420
A fake ceremony?

00:51.420 --> 00:55.280
Then the new Hyral Menas...?

00:55.280 --> 00:57.560
That was a lie, of course.

00:57.560 --> 01:01.860
Our goal was to lure the rats out 
into the open and exterminate them.

01:02.210 --> 01:05.090
So we were just pawns, then?

01:05.090 --> 01:08.290
Then why did His Majesty 
have to face such humiliation?

01:10.720 --> 01:13.390
None of you have meaning! 
None of you have value!

01:13.390 --> 01:17.170
You're all worthless, helpless trash that 
can't do anything but crawl on the ground!

01:17.540 --> 01:18.460
That's so cruel!

01:20.910 --> 01:22.890
Wonderful!

01:23.330 --> 01:28.080
So what you're saying 
is that you're a bad guy

01:28.080 --> 01:32.100
who not only lied to our king, 
but also cut off his arm.

01:32.100 --> 01:34.100
I've got that right, don't I?

01:34.370 --> 01:38.080
Yup. I commend you for your excellent 
understanding of the situation.

01:38.720 --> 01:44.230
Your Majesty, order me to strike 
this criminal down, and I will.

01:44.830 --> 01:46.650
You must not kill him.

01:46.650 --> 01:47.880
Capture him alive.

01:48.210 --> 01:49.590
As you wish.

01:49.990 --> 01:51.560
You heard the man.

01:51.560 --> 01:55.300
So the situation has changed. 
I'll be taking you up on that duel.

01:55.530 --> 01:59.010
Sure, but I've got other 
people to fight today.

01:59.010 --> 02:00.760
Let's make it quick.

02:00.760 --> 02:02.420
Give me all you've got!

02:02.420 --> 02:04.140
Thank you!

02:06.200 --> 02:09.290
<i>Is that pale light... magic?</i>

02:09.290 --> 02:12.190
<i>No, it's nothing I've ever sensed before.</i>

02:12.750 --> 02:16.160
<i>This woman's a threat 
like none I've ever seen...</i>

02:16.490 --> 02:17.150
<i>So I'll...</i>

02:18.260 --> 02:24.570
<i>Come on. The second you touch this wall, 
you'll lose an arm or a leg,</i>

02:24.920 --> 02:28.420
<i>just like that knight and your king did!</i>

02:28.690 --> 02:30.080
What's wrong?

02:30.080 --> 02:31.660
Come and get me.

02:32.130 --> 02:37.720
That magic, it's an "annihilation" effect 
that destroys whatever touches it, right?

02:38.920 --> 02:40.280
<i>How did she know?</i>

02:40.880 --> 02:43.560
<i>Can she see this wall?</i>

02:43.560 --> 02:49.300
It looks like surrounding your whole body 
with it weakened the effects.

02:49.760 --> 02:53.780
It'd be stronger if you concentrated 
your power in one spot.

02:54.210 --> 02:57.530
Go ahead and do that, please.

02:57.530 --> 02:59.750
I'll attack that point.

03:02.580 --> 03:04.030
Are you stupid?

03:04.030 --> 03:09.520
If I do that, and you just attack 
a different spot, I'm finished!

03:09.520 --> 03:12.810
If I wanted to do that, 
I'd already have attacked you.

03:13.850 --> 03:15.880
You can't believe me?

03:16.420 --> 03:21.840
For a Highlander Arch Lord, 
you're kind of a coward.

03:26.570 --> 03:27.980
Nice!

03:27.980 --> 03:29.440
Chris!

03:29.440 --> 03:33.400
Come on! I'll just pray you're not a liar!

03:33.650 --> 03:35.620
Of course! Here I go!

03:37.820 --> 03:42.800
<i>If I use an aether-imbued attack 
to destroy the magic structure itself...</i>

03:52.490 --> 03:54.130
Oops!

03:54.490 --> 03:56.220
Where do you think he fell?

03:56.220 --> 03:58.840
Well, that's Chris for you...

04:14.100 --> 04:17.060
<b><u>Reborn</u></b>

04:14.100 --> 04:17.060
<b>to Master the Blade
\h\h\h\h\hFrom Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire\h\h\h\h\h</b>

04:14.100 --> 04:17.060
<b>to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire</b>

05:30.050 --> 05:34.430
<b>Episode 11      Butt-Kicking Squire</b>

05:40.330 --> 05:47.200
We have no choice now but to 
destroy the Bloodchain Brigade!

05:47.560 --> 05:51.900
We may be able to use that to restore 
relations with the Highland.

05:51.900 --> 05:52.900
Go!

05:52.900 --> 05:53.920
Yes, Your Majesty!

05:53.920 --> 05:56.050
Sire, please evacuate.

05:56.050 --> 05:58.610
Everyone but His Majesty's guards, 
go on the attack!

05:58.610 --> 06:00.190
Yes, sir!

06:00.190 --> 06:03.960
We'll go engage the Bloodchain Brigade, then.

06:03.960 --> 06:05.140
"We"?

06:05.140 --> 06:10.170
Chris, I'm a little tired after 
healing His Majesty's arm...

06:10.650 --> 06:13.440
If you want to rest, you can rest near me.

06:13.440 --> 06:17.450
Wherever you are is bound to be 
where the fighting's fiercest!

06:18.640 --> 06:21.410
It's fine! Come on, come on!

06:21.410 --> 06:24.610
Fine! Fine! Well...

06:24.610 --> 06:27.140
I'll be back later!

06:28.210 --> 06:30.350
She seems like someone I can count on.

06:34.770 --> 06:35.840
Over there!

06:36.220 --> 06:37.660
A Flying Gear!

06:37.660 --> 06:39.540
No time for that!

06:40.490 --> 06:43.100
Sorry to bother you!

06:42.680 --> 06:44.670
Wh-What the heck?!

06:44.670 --> 06:46.230
What <i>is</i> that?

06:46.230 --> 06:48.720
A maid! It's an airborne maid!

06:49.600 --> 06:50.380
She's fast!

06:53.350 --> 06:54.770
There we go.

06:54.770 --> 06:58.440
Look, Rani. We're almost at the 
Bloodchain Brigade's battleship.

06:58.750 --> 07:00.630
I knew it'd be the front line...

07:03.960 --> 07:07.820
We need to stop them now, 
before they hurt more innocents.

07:08.170 --> 07:10.100
Here we go, Chris!

07:10.310 --> 07:13.070
Oh, you're all ready to fight now, huh, Rani?

07:13.070 --> 07:14.830
After seeing that, yeah.

07:15.230 --> 07:17.540
I'll interrupt their attack.

07:17.540 --> 07:19.000
What are you going to do?

07:19.000 --> 07:19.970
Go!

07:20.560 --> 07:21.960
Burst!

07:22.630 --> 07:24.620
Circle the ship!

07:24.620 --> 07:27.530
I see. You're blinding them.

07:27.530 --> 07:32.430
I'll stop their attacks. You stop the ship!

07:32.740 --> 07:34.310
Okay, got it!

07:48.320 --> 07:50.270
Aether Strike!

07:58.480 --> 08:00.390
They deflected it?!

08:06.140 --> 08:07.470
<i>I knew it...</i>

08:09.120 --> 08:11.800
<i>Leon and Sistia don't seem to be there.</i>

08:11.800 --> 08:13.860
That little girl did that?

08:13.860 --> 08:15.760
How can a maid be that powerful?

08:16.250 --> 08:17.940
Welcome.

08:17.940 --> 08:20.730
I'll be serving you this evening.

08:21.200 --> 08:23.930
That was just my way of welcoming you.

08:23.930 --> 08:26.180
S-Serving us?

08:26.180 --> 08:27.620
Be careful.

08:27.620 --> 08:32.400
The more beautiful the rose, the sharper 
its thorns and deadlier its poison.

08:32.900 --> 08:36.630
Continue the mission. I'll deal with her.

08:42.920 --> 08:46.490
What about your plan 
to save the Hyral Menas?

08:47.170 --> 08:51.700
The principal and my friends 
from the academy are handling it.

08:52.310 --> 08:57.410
And if we don't do anything, 
they might think we're with you.

08:58.130 --> 09:02.920
So the two of us came to protect 
the king and the Highlander emissary.

09:03.330 --> 09:10.160
Doesn't splitting your forces make it
more likely that you'll fail on both fronts?

09:10.160 --> 09:14.410
If I take care of things here 
and get over there before they finish,

09:14.410 --> 09:15.870
I get to have twice the fun!

09:16.280 --> 09:17.840
How bold.

09:17.840 --> 09:23.580
While you're being bold, why don't you 
tell me where the Highlander emissary is?

09:23.580 --> 09:26.280
Oh, sorry...

09:28.560 --> 09:30.020
I actually don't know.

09:30.430 --> 09:32.460
That's a shame.

09:33.070 --> 09:35.930
It appears you've grown stronger than before.

09:36.310 --> 09:39.160
I didn't have a way 
of determining that for myself.

09:39.910 --> 09:42.350
But you seem like the perfect opportunity!

09:42.720 --> 09:45.250
So you're using me as a way 
to test yourself?

09:45.990 --> 09:48.070
Thanks in advance!

09:48.070 --> 09:49.910
I guess I have no choice, then.

09:58.610 --> 10:01.110
It seems something did happen at the castle!

10:03.840 --> 10:08.120
All the troops that were escorting Ripple 
headed back to the castle.

10:08.120 --> 10:09.350
Now is our chance.

10:09.350 --> 10:10.820
Okay.

10:10.820 --> 10:16.130
Everyone, I'll say this again: you're under no 
obligation to participate in this operation.

10:16.790 --> 10:19.310
Please don't feel like you have to.

10:19.310 --> 10:21.940
Who's going to go home
after being told <i>that</i>?

10:21.940 --> 10:24.340
Nobody here is going home.

10:24.980 --> 10:27.940
Actually, in that case, 
I'm gonna go home and sleep.

10:28.830 --> 10:31.740
Wait! Wait, Yua!

10:32.010 --> 10:34.450
We need you here!

10:34.450 --> 10:37.120
You just said I didn't have to do it.

10:37.660 --> 10:41.440
We need your help. 
Please lend us your aid.

10:41.730 --> 10:43.960
Mr. Glasses, do you have a fever?

10:43.960 --> 10:44.750
No!

10:44.750 --> 10:45.970
I'm just fine!

10:45.970 --> 10:48.350
Oh, you're right. You get mad so fast.

10:48.350 --> 10:50.360
Depending on who I'm talking to!

10:51.730 --> 10:54.580
This isn't the time! 
We're about to start the mission!

10:54.580 --> 10:56.420
I'm asking you to stay, too.

10:57.070 --> 10:58.980
I could really use you on my side.

11:00.400 --> 11:01.720
Ripple...

11:02.130 --> 11:07.180
I thought I had no choice but to accept 
what was happening to me.

11:08.370 --> 11:12.940
A Hyral Menas who can't protect anyone... 
is no Hyral Menas at all.

11:13.610 --> 11:19.520
But you're all doing your absolute best 
to protect me, right?

11:20.120 --> 11:23.660
Well, one of you seems 
to just be having fun.

11:23.660 --> 11:27.120
True. I won't say who, though.

11:27.570 --> 11:29.940
She's probably sneezing right now.

11:29.940 --> 11:32.220
I'm sure she is.

11:40.080 --> 11:44.490
The home where I was born 
was destroyed years and years ago.

11:45.250 --> 11:49.800
But now this country is my home. 
I can really feel that now.

11:50.330 --> 11:52.380
I understand how I really feel...

11:53.060 --> 11:55.090
I know I'm causing trouble for you all,

11:55.090 --> 11:57.360
but I want to stay here with 
the people of this country.

11:58.110 --> 12:03.450
So... it's only natural that 
I'd ask for help, right?

12:03.900 --> 12:05.070
Ripple...

12:05.560 --> 12:07.620
So, Yua...

12:07.620 --> 12:10.050
Yua, Ripple is begging for your help—

12:10.050 --> 12:11.780
Zzz...

12:11.780 --> 12:13.530
Hey!

12:14.030 --> 12:15.480
He's interrupting my sleep!

12:15.480 --> 12:17.490
Save me, Lady Animal Ears!

12:17.490 --> 12:21.100
Anyway, I want your help.

12:21.100 --> 12:24.480
If it works out, I'll buy you dinner, okay?

12:24.480 --> 12:29.170
I don't want food. I want you to 
introduce me to somebody.

12:31.330 --> 12:33.170
What kind of person?

12:33.170 --> 12:35.630
Somebody as cool as Mr. Glasses.

12:36.430 --> 12:39.850
Wh-What? It's too late for you to try 
and get on my good side—

12:39.850 --> 12:45.080
Somebody who's not as short-tempered 
or weak as Mr. Glasses...

12:45.080 --> 12:46.830
Why, you...

12:47.150 --> 12:52.500
Okay, now that we've made it to the 
punchline, I'd like to start the mission!

12:52.500 --> 12:55.050
The <i>punchline</i>? Ma'am...

12:55.050 --> 12:57.590
Go ahead, Leone.

12:57.590 --> 12:58.400
Okay!

13:06.030 --> 13:11.840
Principal Miliera and I will have Ripple 
absorb our power and summon magicite beasts.

13:12.310 --> 13:15.630
You take them out when they show up!

13:22.560 --> 13:24.980
It's in your hands, everyone.

13:33.810 --> 13:36.910
Spread out in a circle around Ripple!

13:52.230 --> 13:53.170
Here they come!

14:04.820 --> 14:06.560
<i>Such incredible power!</i>

14:07.210 --> 14:10.740
<i>I can see why you're the leader 
of the Bloodchain Brigade!</i>

14:13.750 --> 14:16.250
Chris, I believe in you!

14:25.420 --> 14:28.510
Sorry. I'm not done yet.

14:29.100 --> 14:30.580
That's more than fine by me!

14:32.110 --> 14:37.180
<i>I can sense one more aether flow, 
besides his Aether Shell.</i>

14:40.760 --> 14:42.220
An aether sword?

14:42.620 --> 14:46.690
I'm amazed you dodged that. Impressive.

14:46.690 --> 14:51.410
That sword's made of compressed 
and stabilized aether, isn't it?

14:52.060 --> 14:55.740
<i>I can use magic to create a sword too, but...</i>

14:57.740 --> 15:04.360
<i>Wielding a compressed aether sword and 
aether armor simultaneously is no mean feat.</i>

15:04.360 --> 15:07.020
<i>I can't do that myself yet.</i>

15:07.020 --> 15:08.730
It is as you say.

15:08.730 --> 15:10.060
Sorry, but you're mine!

15:16.210 --> 15:18.380
<i>At this distance, he has the advantage.</i>

15:18.380 --> 15:20.960
<i>I need to get closer!</i>

15:20.960 --> 15:22.310
<i>But that sword...</i>

15:22.690 --> 15:28.700
<i>If I take a hit from that, even with my 
Aether Shell, I won't be getting off lightly.</i>

15:29.320 --> 15:30.570
<i>Which means...</i>

15:30.860 --> 15:32.370
<i>I've got one chance!</i>

15:34.470 --> 15:37.570
That weak blade can't stop me!

15:37.570 --> 15:39.540
It doesn't need to!

15:40.130 --> 15:43.200
<i>If it can halt him for even 
a second, I can get close!</i>

15:49.050 --> 15:50.590
Aether Strike!

15:57.450 --> 16:00.300
She's approaching the point 
where even I can't stop her?

16:00.930 --> 16:06.520
It sounds like you've been busy. 
But I've been focusing on training.

16:06.520 --> 16:09.510
Chris, something's coming! Focus!

16:12.980 --> 16:16.040
Ivel! I'm so glad you're okay!

16:16.040 --> 16:20.280
What? You were the one who 
kicked me into the sky!

16:20.280 --> 16:25.060
Arch Lord... You're the emissary this time?

16:25.060 --> 16:28.330
So you're the leader 
of the Bloodchain Brigade?

16:28.330 --> 16:30.250
What a stupid-looking costume.

16:30.250 --> 16:35.400
Get back, Ivel. He's after your life.

16:35.400 --> 16:37.530
That's exactly what I want!

16:37.820 --> 16:41.850
I'm going to crush their leader, 
before moving on to the rest of the maggots!

16:41.850 --> 16:46.060
Then I suppose I'll need to defend myself.

16:46.340 --> 16:50.410
Wait! That's no reason to fight each other!

16:50.410 --> 16:52.040
Why can't we all just get along?

16:52.040 --> 16:53.790
You're one to talk!

16:54.180 --> 16:58.140
Of course, if you'd both like to fight me...

16:58.140 --> 17:00.030
I've secured the bridge.

17:00.460 --> 17:02.700
Well done, Sistia.

17:02.700 --> 17:05.300
Things have become rather complicated.

17:05.920 --> 17:09.620
Sistia, lend me your strength.

17:09.620 --> 17:10.990
With pleasure.

17:12.350 --> 17:16.960
My power, my being... Use them as you like.

17:16.960 --> 17:19.810
I entrust it all to you.

17:20.410 --> 17:22.370
The Hyral Menas is becoming a weapon?

17:22.370 --> 17:23.640
Not if I can help it!

17:37.910 --> 17:39.470
Amazing!

17:40.470 --> 17:45.070
<i>It's absorbing aether, 
rather than mana, and amplifying it!</i>

17:45.490 --> 17:48.980
<i>The Hyral Menas lives up to their reputation!</i>

17:50.400 --> 17:51.470
Gotcha.

17:57.350 --> 18:01.130
You really are amazing, Yua.

18:01.130 --> 18:03.050
Thank you, Curly Hair.

18:03.050 --> 18:05.280
But I'm a little tired...

18:05.280 --> 18:08.340
I think we're at our limits.

18:21.750 --> 18:23.200
Leone...

18:23.200 --> 18:24.490
Thank you!

18:28.280 --> 18:30.160
Nice, Two.

18:30.530 --> 18:34.370
She's using her spatial isolation Gift 
at the same time... Well done.

18:34.370 --> 18:37.540
Thank you.

18:37.540 --> 18:42.170
But... sorry. I think I'm at my limit...

18:47.050 --> 18:49.180
Is this all we can do?

18:49.180 --> 18:52.060
Let's defeat the magicite beasts 
in front of us, at least!

18:57.320 --> 18:58.240
No!

19:00.900 --> 19:03.410
Lightning beasts? Is that...

19:07.650 --> 19:09.100
Brother?

19:09.880 --> 19:10.710
Hey.

19:10.710 --> 19:14.540
So, um... I'm sure you have a lot 
you want to say to me.

19:15.080 --> 19:17.010
But I'm going to help you.

19:18.650 --> 19:21.390
Hey, don't look so mad.

19:21.390 --> 19:24.710
You saw that, right? I'm here to help.

19:25.090 --> 19:28.970
Do you know how much Leone has suffered?

19:29.700 --> 19:33.150
Do you think you can atone 
by helping us here?

19:33.150 --> 19:35.320
I understand.

19:35.320 --> 19:36.600
Here.

19:39.560 --> 19:41.960
What is that?

19:41.960 --> 19:43.500
Mana mist.

19:43.500 --> 19:45.350
It should help you.

19:46.420 --> 19:49.450
He's right... My body feels so light...

19:50.170 --> 19:52.410
That's a big help!

19:52.410 --> 19:56.210
Yeah, my new boss has a lot 
of helpful stuff.

19:56.210 --> 19:59.650
He's the one who told me 
to come here, actually.

20:01.380 --> 20:04.700
You shouldn't keep your desire for justice 
bottled up within you.

20:05.450 --> 20:09.150
If there's something you want 
to protect, go protect it.

20:09.800 --> 20:12.560
So I didn't have a choice. No choice at all.

20:12.560 --> 20:14.770
"No choice"?

20:15.230 --> 20:18.050
Leone, seal us all in pocket space again.

20:19.360 --> 20:21.430
You're still doubting me?

20:21.430 --> 20:23.520
I'm not going to try and trick you.

20:23.520 --> 20:25.190
I-I know!

20:25.710 --> 20:31.000
You're actually a little glad 
I'm here, aren't you?

20:31.700 --> 20:33.250
I am not!

20:43.330 --> 20:45.900
You're feeding mana to Ripple, right?

20:49.300 --> 20:50.520
Silva...

20:50.520 --> 20:51.300
Right.

20:51.300 --> 20:54.020
Get ready, everybody.

21:25.010 --> 21:26.760
Chris! Look!

21:26.760 --> 21:29.040
It's from the direction of the academy.

21:39.590 --> 21:41.310
Hey, you okay?

21:41.310 --> 21:44.040
Brother, what was that?

21:44.320 --> 21:45.460
Look.

21:53.460 --> 21:57.430
Ripple summoned something unbelievable.

22:03.290 --> 22:06.090
That's... a Prismer!

23:44.980 --> 23:49.980
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

23:44.980 --> 23:49.980
Don't you wish
 we could've
 worn cute
 outfits too?

23:44.980 --> 23:49.980
Comic by Kuromura Moto
